From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Duke Eagleman <301139544+jerricky26@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: s8000-mca: Run the T8010 I2S frame from prepare

The CS42L83 on the T8010 headphone link derives its MCLK from SCLK with
its PLL, and cs42l42_mute_stream() starts and locks that PLL when ASoC
unmutes the stream, which happens at the end of prepare, before
trigger. This driver only set FRAME RUN at trigger, so the PLL never
locked; the codec then switched to the dead PLL anyway, its control port
lost its clock and stopped answering, and on J171 the stalled transfer
wedged i2c0, which it shares with the PMIC and charger.

Start the provider frame at prepare for this variant. It already keeps
running until hw_free, after the codec has been muted and moved back to
its internal oscillator. The MAX98357A speaker link is unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 sound/soc/apple/s8000-mca.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/s8000-mca.c b/sound/soc/apple/s8000-mca.c
--- a/sound/soc/apple/s8000-mca.c
+++ b/sound/soc/apple/s8000-mca.c
@@ -143,6 +143,12 @@
 struct s8000_mca_hw {
 	u32 version;
 	bool clock_provider;
+	/*
+	 * Run the provider frame from prepare, not trigger: a codec that
+	 * clocks itself from SCLK (CS42L42 family) locks its PLL when ASoC
+	 * unmutes it, which is after prepare and before trigger.
+	 */
+	bool clocks_at_prepare;
 	unsigned int dai_format;	/* SND_SOC_DAIFMT_* */
 	unsigned int channels;
 	unsigned int slots;
@@ -516,7 +522,8 @@
 			   MCA_IRQ_RX_CAUSES);
 	mca_write(mca, MCA_IRQ_MASK, mca->irq_mask);
 	if (first)
-		mca_write(mca, MCA_FRAME, mca->frame);
+		mca_write(mca, MCA_FRAME, mca->frame |
+			  (mca->hw->clocks_at_prepare ? MCA_FRAME_RUN : 0));
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&mca->hw_lock, flags);
 
 	if (first)
@@ -861,6 +868,7 @@
 static const struct s8000_mca_hw t8010_i2s_mca_hw = {
 	.version = 5,
 	.clock_provider = true,
+	.clocks_at_prepare = true,
 	.dai_format = SND_SOC_DAIFMT_I2S,
 	.channels = 2,
 	.slots = 2,
-- 
